TVbomb's right. It might make sense to add daily hair,skin, or blood sampling. Precise telomeric age identification may or may not be in the Foundation's abilities today, but is likely not far off, and having samples since maybe 2007 would be useful in constructing a timeline for him. Also, even with techniques as subtle as an insulin tester, it would be ironic (always feel like I'm misusing that&#8230;) if the modern Foundation was oblivious to its own additions to Vladimir's tribulations.<br />
Monday-2017-Doctor has me sprayed down and deloused, then takes samples.Always more samples.<br />
Tuesday-1952-Beaten for my name(even though I'll be born in [redacted]), accused of communism, drugged.<br />
Wednesday-????-Blurry from yesterday's drugs. Beaten for some reason. Something about rice and flowers.<br />
Thursday-1760- Some Inn. Beaten, driven out of town as a witch.<br />
Friday-1865- Prison again, 30 lashes for waking up outside my cell.<br />
Saturday-????-Slave to the giant hairy men. Not so bad, but they make us sleep together in kennels.<br />
Sunday-1930-Sideshow freak. Made to sleep while kids throw things at me.Punishments don't make sleep easier.<br />
Repeat. I hate needles.</p>

